The existence check for a particular user is vulnerable to a blind SQL injection attack where characters from the
password of natas16 can be checked one character at a time.  By injecting a rogue "AND password REGEXP "^[a-zA-Z0-9]" ..
as part of the username query, we can figure out what the password for natas16 begins with.  Note that the encoding
of the database is such that queries are fuzzy (i.e. case insensitive).  As part of our SQL query, we must include
"COLLATE latin1_general_cs" to ensure a match.

The password for natas16 is WaIHEacj63wnNIBROHeqi3p9t0m5nhmh

Script to do a single blind sql query is in 15/blindsql.py